  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "數位鑑識",
    "sub_ename": "DIGITAL FORENSICS",
    "describe_ch": "依照資訊安全事件應對措施，依時間軸分為事前、事中、事後三個階段，數位鑑識為事後階段的處理應用方法之一。即便已有相關技術與工具，但在不了解數位鑑識標準作業程序的情形下，容易造成證據的破壞，將直接破壞其證據能力，無法成為資安事件之佐證，若為民事或刑事事件，則無法成為呈堂供證。本課程除了從各個技術面向討論與實作數位鑑識，亦將強調數位鑑識標準作業程序，培養同學正確的數位鑑識執行觀念。",
    "describe_eh": "According to the information security incident response measures, the timeline is divided into three stages: before, during, and after the incident. Digital forensics is one of the processing application methods in the post-incident stage. Even if the relevant technology and tools are available, if one does not understand the digital forensics standard operating procedures, it is easy to cause the destruction of evidence, which will directly undermine its evidentiary capacity and make it impossible to serve as evidence in cybersecurity incidents. In civil or criminal cases, it cannot be presented as evidence in court. In addition to discussing and implementing digital forensics from various technical aspects, this course will also emphasize digital forensics standard operating procedures to cultivate students' correct digital forensics implementation concepts.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 3.0
  },
